# Project knowledge

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-01 -->
Read the basic constraints and standards routing in AGENTS.md, then use the confirmed Harness root and .lumine/project.json configuration. The default Wiki root is docs/repo-wiki/; configuration is authoritative. The nearest Git root is not necessarily a multi-repository Harness root. Retrieval never replaces mandatory project rules.

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-02 -->
Choose the knowledge map, section search, direct Markdown reading, or source inspection according to the question. No mandatory Wiki-first step or tool-call quota applies. When useful, use `wiki map / query / show / related` to expand selectively. Results are limited to six and a context budget; inspect scope, provenance, and freshness, and reformulate Chinese, English, or code-identifier queries as needed. See [Investigation and retrieval](references/investigation.md).

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-03 -->
For initialization, read [Understanding and building](references/building.md). Cover all major modules in depth by default with a project-specific hierarchy; users may narrow or defer the scope. During adoption/upgrades, also read [Adoption delivery and acceptance](references/delivery.md); use [Service extensions](references/services.md) when needed. For maintenance, read [Knowledge maintenance](references/maintenance.md). The Agent/model interprets sources, assesses semantic impact, and writes prose and Mermaid. `scan` supplies change clues; `update` validates and safely saves Agent-authored text without calling a model to produce knowledge. Without an active Agent, only pending work can be registered.

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-04 -->
Body text, summaries, Mermaid text, and sources form one shared content set for people and Agents. Cards use HTML DOM; diagrams render on demand in the browser. Scanning, generation, updates, queries, and review use text only: no image generation, screenshot recognition, vision models, card images, thumbnail files, or rendered SVG in model input. Copy and export Markdown or Mermaid text. Dedicated browser UI verification is separate from the knowledge pipeline.

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-05 -->
Semantic review verifies actual sources and material relationships. Product Spec describes product goals, scope, scenarios, rules, and acceptance; Exec Plan derives technical approach, tradeoffs, execution arrangements, progress, and records from Specs/AC items. Wiki distinguishes known implementation, confirmed domain language and lasting decisions, usage guides, AGENTS-authorized standards, and explanatory examples. Confirmed language does not prove implementation, and unimplemented proposals are not current facts. Ordinary synchronization cannot relax standards or authorization based on legacy code; review affected content after standards change. Label inferred rationale and distinguish source from deployment or observation.

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-06 -->
Organize topics as answer, mechanism and diagrams, tradeoffs and limits, then sources. Stable sections expose concrete mechanisms and constraints, beyond whole-page introductions. The hierarchy, pages, sections, and cards share body text and the knowledge map; split complex topics. After investigating missing, stale, or contradictory content, write reusable verified findings back within authorization; explicit read-only requests receive a report only. No knowledge change is required when none was learned, and queries need no compulsory log. Protect human edits, useful candidates, and conflicts.

<!-- LH-KNOWLEDGE-07 -->
When asked to open the knowledge base or start, restart, or stop its reader, read [Reader management](references/reader.md). Prefer reusing a service owned by the current project, and verify process ownership before stopping it. Direct Markdown reading and Agent retrieval need no server.
